NAFA merged prototype — third-party dependency inventory
=======================================================

The repository's LICENSE covers project code. Third-party packages, models and
input documents retain their own licenses and terms; they are not relicensed by
the repository license. No model weights are included in this repository.

Runtime versions are locked in src/store/uv.lock and src/report_scripts/uv.lock.
The unified image installs the store lock and imports the PE and DA source code.

Core runtime:
- FastAPI, HTTPX, Pydantic, APScheduler, PyYAML: MIT
- Uvicorn, pandas, NumPy, SciPy, scikit-learn: BSD-style licenses
- Beautiful Soup: MIT; lxml: BSD-style license, plus its bundled library notices
- pymorphy3 and Russian dictionaries: retain installed package/dictionary notices
- PyMuPDF: upstream AGPL/commercial licensing; see its installed distribution
  and src/store/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES

Preparation and verification:
- matplotlib: upstream Matplotlib license and bundled notices
- tabulate, pytest, uv: retain their upstream licenses
- Playwright: Apache-2.0; the locally installed browser has separate terms
- Optional Tesseract OCR/language data: upstream notices, when installed

Full license texts remain in the installed packages' dist-info/licenses or
equivalent metadata directories and in any bundled browser/system packages.
The list above is an inventory, not an assertion that all redistribution or
deployment requirements have been fulfilled. Confirm the licenses of the exact
distribution when creating the final external deliverable.

Supplied bank PDFs, corpus extraction, CSV data and source articles are input
materials. Their inclusion here does not grant rights beyond those provided by
their owners or the case organisers. Secrets and participant CSVs are excluded
from the Git and Docker contexts.
